From db870cf1cb996d17e6b6d860a7ced320e1c6fa1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OLS-cPanel-WHM <2tdv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:15:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close the detached worker's listener after handing it to
 lscgid

startDetachedWorker() creates a new listening socket for every detached
(runOnStartUp 3) lsapi process group and passes it to lscgid, but the
server kept its own copy open. Every group start leaked one descriptor,
and the leaked copy kept the socket of an exiting group alive: a
connection queued on it while the group's parent was shutting down was
never accepted and never reset, so the request hung until the
connection timeout ("No request delivery notification has been received
from LSAPI application, possible dead lock"). Close it, as upstream
1.9.4 does.
---
 src/extensions/localworker.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/extensions/localworker.cpp b/src/extensions/localworker.cpp
index 56e01a6..aea6948 100644
--- a/src/extensions/localworker.cpp
+++ b/src/extensions/localworker.cpp
@@ -1108,6 +1108,8 @@ TRY_AGAIN:
 
 
     pid = workerExec(config, fd);
+    // SCM_RIGHTS gives lscgid its own descriptor; do not retain the listener.
+    close(fd);
     if (pid != 0)
     {
         ret = processPid(pid, service_addr.getUnix());
-- 
